    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169-a2">

                <pb facs="0377" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg357"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr.
                        Thurston.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 61.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 16, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch, No. 95, has been received.
                    The spirit manifested by the Canadian ministers at the conference to which it
                    relates was just and friendly; we hope they may arrest the evil. Your own
                    proceedings are approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FREDERICK W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. Thurston,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >United States Vice-Consul General, Montreal.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
